{
  "name": "bicycle",
  "doc": "A bicycle with a diamond frame from its geometry sheet, built by the people of each trade at the same time: a welder makes the frame and the fork from the numbers of the sheet, wheelwrights the two wheels, a mechanic the crankset with its pedals, smiths the rack and the kickstand. The defaults are a touring frame of 54 cm on tires of 700 x 35c. The origin is on the ground at the center of the bike; the front is to +y.",
  "sources": [
    "A touring frame of 54 cm: chainstay 430 mm, bottom bracket drop 70 mm, stack 580 mm, reach 380 mm, head angle 72 degrees, seat angle 73.5 degrees, rake 45 mm; the numbers of a geometry sheet of a maker are the params, and the wheelbase is a result of them."
  ],
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "name",
      "type": "text",
      "default": "bicycle",
      "max": 40,
      "doc": "The name of the model: a to z, 0 to 9 and _."
    },
    {
      "name": "tire",
      "type": "text",
      "default": "37-622",
      "doc": "The code of the tires (ETRTO).",
      "max": 20
    },
    {
      "name": "spokes",
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 36,
      "min": 16,
      "max": 48,
      "doc": "The spokes of each wheel."
    },
    {
      "name": "chainstay",
      "type": "number",
      "default": 0.43,
      "min": 0.35,
      "max": 0.55,
      "unit": "m",
      "doc": "From the bottom bracket to the rear axle."
    },
    {
